IMPORT prelude

-- Government Technology Agency Act 2016 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person or business it touches: the
-- Agency's symbol (s 9), the secrecy duty and who it binds (s 43), protection from personal liability (s 44), the
-- composition cap (s 68), officers' liability for a corporation's offence (s 69), service of documents (s 71), member
-- disqualification, vacation of office and quorum (ss 12(2), 21(1)(g), 31), and the reach of the Agency's security powers
-- over the public sector and over private "public entities" (ss 2, 61, 62, 64 to 67).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GTAA2016.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021";
-- the retrieval record calls it the current version as at 1 October 2026. The latest amendment annotated in the text is
-- G.N. No. S 461/2020 (Variable Capital Companies (Consequential Amendments to Other Acts) Order 2020, in force 15 June
-- 2020); the other is Act 5 of 2018 (Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018, s 64, in force 1 April 2018).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0171 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario
-- has asked a sharper question yet. Most of the Act constitutes a statutory board; this row takes the provisions an
-- outsider, an employee or an essential-service company can actually meet.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: objectives, functions and general powers (ss 5 to 8) beyond what the security Parts rely on; appointment,
-- chair, removal, resignation and terms of members (ss 10, 11, 13 to 20, 22); meetings, voting, seal, committees and
-- delegation (ss 28 to 39); personnel (s 40); finance (ss 45 to 53); s 70 (unincorporated associations and partnerships,
-- which mirrors s 69); exclusion of public authorities and regulations (ss 72, 73); the 2016 transfer from IDA (Parts 10
-- and 11). No regulations under s 73 were retrieved, so which offences are "prescribed as compoundable" is unknown.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Government Technology Agency Act 2016 -- persons`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `9 -- the Agency's symbol`

-- s 9(1): the Agency "has the exclusive right to the use of one or more symbols or representations as it may select or
-- devise". (2): a person who "(a) uses, without the prior written permission of the Agency, a symbol or representation that
-- is identical with the Agency's symbol or representation; or (b) uses a symbol or representation that so resembles the
-- Agency's symbol or representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion"
-- commits an offence: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both".
-- The words "without the prior written permission" appear only in para (a). Read literally, permission is no answer to
-- para (b). That is how it is encoded.
GIVEN `uses an identical symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `had prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `uses a confusingly similar symbol` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the symbol is an offence` IF
        (`uses an identical symbol` AND (NOT `had prior written permission`))
    OR  `uses a confusingly similar symbol`

§§ `43 and 44 -- secrecy and protection from personal liability`

-- s 43(1): "The Chief Executive, a member, an employee or a delegate of the Agency, or a committee member, who has
-- information in his or her capacity as such that would not otherwise be available to him or her, must not disclose that
-- information to any person except -- (a) in the performance of the Agency's functions; (b) with the prior authorisation
-- from the Agency to do so; (c) in complying with the requirements in this Act for a member of the Agency or a committee
-- member to disclose an interest; (d) as required or allowed by this Act or any other Act; or (e) as required by an order of
-- court." (2): "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both".
-- s 2: "employee" means (outside Part 10) "an individual who is employed by the Agency under a contract of service or who is
-- otherwise engaged to perform duties in the Agency".
-- s 44: no liability lies against the same five classes "or any other person acting under the direction of the Agency, for
-- anything which is done or purported to be done, or omitted to be done, in good faith and with reasonable care".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `the Chief Executive`
    `a member of the Agency`
    `an employee under a contract of service`
    `a contractor engaged to perform duties in the Agency`
    `a delegate of the Agency`
    `a committee member who is not a member of the Agency`
    `a vendor acting under the direction of the Agency`
    `a member of the public`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is bound by the secrecy duty` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a vendor acting under the direction of the Agency` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a member of the public` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `performing the Agency's functions`
    `with the Agency's prior authorisation`
    `disclosing an interest as the Act requires`
    `as required or allowed by an Act`
    `under an order of court`
    `telling a journalist`
    `telling a friend`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an excepted disclosure` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `telling a journalist` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `telling a friend` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `had it only in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `is bound by the secrecy duty` `the person`
    AND `had it only in that capacity`
    AND (NOT `is an excepted disclosure` `the purpose`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is protected from personal liability` IF
        (NOT (`the person` EQUALS `a member of the public`))
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `acted with reasonable care`

§§ `9, 43 and 68 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 68(1): the Chief Executive, or an authorised employee, "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the
-- maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000." (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken".
-- s 47: composition sums go to the Consolidated Fund.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Agency's symbol`
    `breaching secrecy`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Agency's symbol` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Agency's symbol` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition may collect` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `69 -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 69(2): where a corporation commits an offence under this Act, a person "(a) who is -- (i) an officer of the
-- corporation; or (ii) an individual involved in the management of the corporation and in a position to influence the
-- conduct of the corporation in relation to the commission of the offence; and (b) who -- (i) consented or connived, or
-- conspired with others ...; (ii) is in any other way ... knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the commission ...; or
-- (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have known that the offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to take all
-- reasonable steps to prevent or stop the commission of that offence, shall be guilty of that same offence".
-- (5): it applies "whether or not the corporation is convicted". s 70 says the same of associations and partnerships.
GIVEN `is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an influential manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN, `was knowingly concerned` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty of the same offence` IF
        (`is an officer` OR `is an influential manager`)
    AND (    `consented, connived or conspired`
         OR  `was knowingly concerned`
         OR  (`knew or ought to have known` AND (NOT `took all reasonable steps`)))

§§ `71 -- service of documents on an individual`

-- s 71(2): a document may be served on an individual "(a) by giving it to the individual personally; (b) by sending it by
-- prepaid registered post to the address specified by the individual ... or ... the individual's residential address or
-- business address; (c) by leaving it at the individual's residential address with an adult apparently resident there, or
-- at the individual's business address with an adult apparently employed there; (d) by affixing a copy ... in a
-- conspicuous place at the individual's residential address or business address; (e) by ... fax to the fax number given by
-- the individual ...; or (f) by sending it by email to the individual's email address" -- defined in (7) as "the last email
-- address given by the addressee ... as the email address for the service of documents under this Act".
-- (5)(c): registered post takes effect "2 days after the day the document was posted (even if it is returned undelivered)".
-- (6): "this section does not apply to documents to be served in proceedings in court".
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `handing it over personally`
    `prepaid registered post to the home address`
    `leaving it with an adult living at the home`
    `affixing it to the front door`
    `ordinary post`
    `email to an address given for service`
    `a text message`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a way to serve an individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `ordinary post` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a text message` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `day posted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day registered post takes effect` MEANS
    `day posted` PLUS 2

GIVEN `is for court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 71 governs the service` IF
    NOT `is for court proceedings`

§§ `12(2), 21(1)(g) and 31 -- sitting on the Agency`

-- s 12(2): disqualified are "(a) a Judge or judicial officer; (b) an undischarged bankrupt; (c) an individual who has been
-- sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more, and has not received a free pardon; (d)" an individual
-- disqualified as a company or VCC director (Companies Act 1967 ss 149, 149A, 154; Variable Capital Companies Act 2018
-- ss 56 to 58); "(e) an individual who lacks capacity ... within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008, or in respect
-- of whom an order is made under section 10 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008".
GIVEN `is a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER, `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a disqualified director` IS A BOOLEAN, `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is disqualified from membership` IF
        `is a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `is a disqualified director`
    OR  `lacks capacity`

-- s 21(1)(g): a member ceases to hold office if he or she "fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Agency without the
-- approval of the Agency".
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed` IS A NUMBER, `the Agency approved the absences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member ceases to hold office` IF
    `consecutive meetings missed` AT LEAST 3 AND (NOT `the Agency approved the absences`)

-- s 31(1): "The quorum for a meeting of the Agency is the higher of the following: (a) one-third of the number of members;
-- (b) 3 members." (2): no business without a quorum. Encoded without rounding: present times 3 must reach the membership.
GIVEN `members in office` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members in office` AND `members present` AT LEAST 3

§§ `2, 61, 62, 64 to 67 -- the Agency's reach over public bodies and public entities`

-- s 2: "public authority" means a body established under a public Act to discharge a public function, "but does not
-- include a Town Council"; "public sector" means "the Government and all public authorities"; "public entity" means "a
-- body corporate (not being a public authority) that -- (a) provides an essential service to the public or a section of
-- the public; and (b) receives funding or other facilities or support from the Government in connection with" it.
-- s 61(2): the Agency may audit "any info-communications technology or related engineering system or service in the public
-- sector". s 62(1): where the Agency thinks more is needed, it "may, with the authorisation of the Minister -- (a)
-- implement, or direct the public sector body responsible ... to implement, any security, mitigation or recovery measures".
-- s 67: over a designated public entity, and "Subject to the arrangements established and approved under section 66", the
-- Agency may recommend directives, "carry out an audit, or require an audit to be carried out", "advise" on measures and on
-- resources, and report -- it is given no power to direct.
-- INFERENCE: a Town Council, being excluded from "public authority", is outside the "public sector" as defined. The text
-- does not say so in terms; "public sector body" also covers "any other body of persons in the public sector".
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `a Ministry`
    `a statutory board`
    `a Town Council`
    `a designated public entity`
    `a public entity not designated`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the public sector` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a Ministry` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body, `the Minister authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Agency thinks more measures are needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may direct the body to take measures` IF
        `is in the public sector` `the body`
    AND `the Minister authorised it`
    AND `the Agency thinks more measures are needed`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body, `the arrangements cover an audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may audit the body's systems` IF
        `is in the public sector` `the body`
    OR  ((`the body` EQUALS `a designated public entity`) AND `the arrangements cover an audit`)

GIVEN `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `provides an essential service` IS A BOOLEAN, `receives Government support for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a public entity` IF
        `is a body corporate`
    AND (NOT `is a public authority`)
    AND `provides an essential service`
    AND `receives Government support for it`

-- s 65: a responsible Minister may request the Agency's help for a public entity if of the opinion that "(a) the security
-- or reliability of the system or service is at significant risk or has been significantly compromised; and (b) it is in
-- the public interest, or in the interest of public safety or the security of Singapore". s 66: the Agency's Minister may
-- then direct arrangements, which the responsible Minister approves, followed by a Gazette declaration (s 66(3)).
GIVEN `the system is at significant risk or compromised` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is in the public interest, safety or security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the responsible Minister may request the Agency's help` IF
    `the system is at significant risk or compromised` AND `it is in the public interest, safety or security`
